    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n104235" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τολμ-ητός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, also <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ός</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>
		<i><span class="en">
			E.
			<u>Hel.</u>
			816
		</span></i>:—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>ventured,
				to be ventured,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πὰν τόλμᾱτον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Sapph.
					2.17
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔστ᾽ ἐκείνῳ πάντα . . τολμητά</span>”
				<i>within the compass of his daring,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Ph.</u>
					634
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Cratin.
				324b
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐλπὶς τ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
				</span></i>
			 l. c.</div>
